[SIZE=5][B]World editing for Paper that never lags the server[/B][/SIZE]
Every edit, from ten blocks to ten million, runs in small batches inside a time budget shared by the whole plugin. Preview it before it happens, undo it even after a restart (without erasing what others built since), write patterns the way you would say them, and make a mountain or a floating island with one word. You do not need WorldEdit: Worldcraft has its own engine, its own .schem reader and writer, and [B]138 commands[/B] under /wc, which also work the WorldEdit way: //set, //copy -e, /brush, //undo.[/CENTER]

[I]Worldcraft is not affiliated with or endorsed by EngineHub (WorldEdit), IntellectualSites (FastAsyncWorldEdit) or Mojang.[/I]

[SIZE=5][B]How it compares[/B][/SIZE]
Counted from the @Command annotations inside the WorldEdit 7.3.19 and FAWE 2.16.2 jars (sub-commands included), and counting only what Worldcraft does the same or better:
[LIST]
[*][B]WorldEdit 7.3.19:[/B] 171 commands. Worldcraft has [B]157[/B] (92 %), 5 more in part.
[*][B]FastAsyncWorldEdit 2.16.2:[/B] 244 commands. Worldcraft has [B]205[/B] (84 %), 13 more in part.
[*][B]Worldcraft 0.16.0:[/B] [B]138[/B] under /wc (212 counted like WorldEdit counts its own).
[/LIST]
Every command, one by one, with its Worldcraft equivalent: [URL='https://github.com/leonardos4enz/fabrica-de-plugins/blob/main/docs/worldcraft/presentacion/commands.md']commands.md[/URL].

[LIST]
[*][B]Big edits never lag the server:[/B] Worldcraft yes (8 ms per tick, shared) · WorldEdit no (main thread) · FAWE yes (async, server internals)
[*][B]See the result before it changes:[/B] Worldcraft yes ([FONT=Courier New]--preview[/FONT], only you) · WorldEdit no · FAWE no
[*][B]See the selection without a client mod:[/B] Worldcraft yes (particles) · WorldEdit and FAWE need the CUI mod
[*][B]Undo after a restart:[/B] Worldcraft yes (on disk) · WorldEdit no · FAWE yes
[*][B]Undo leaves what others built since:[/B] Worldcraft yes · WorldEdit no · FAWE no
[*][B]Safe limits out of the box:[/B] Worldcraft yes (50 000 blocks by default) · WorldEdit no limit · FAWE per group
[*][B]Mountains and floating islands in one word:[/B] only Worldcraft
[*][B]Patterns in plain words, "did you mean":[/B] Worldcraft yes · WorldEdit and FAWE in part
[*][B]Shapes, brushes, tools, formulas, biomes, regen, snapshots:[/B] all three
[*][B]WorldEdit .schem files (v1, v2, v3):[/B] all three (Worldcraft reads and writes them)
[*][B]Caves, ores, pictures (from FAWE):[/B] Worldcraft and FAWE
[*][B]Only the Paper API (no server internals):[/B] Worldcraft and WorldEdit
[*][B]Used by WorldGuard and PlotSquared:[/B] WorldEdit and FAWE (keep WorldEdit for them)
[/LIST]

[SIZE=5][B]Commands (138)[/B][/SIZE]
Everything is [FONT=Courier New]/wc <command>[/FONT] (or [FONT=Courier New]/worldcraft[/FONT]); [FONT=Courier New]/wc help <command>[/FONT] shows how to use each one with an example.
[LIST]
[*][B]Select (16):[/B] [FONT=Courier New]/wc wand, pos1, pos2, hpos1, hpos2, sel[/FONT] (cuboid, extend, poly, ellipsoid, sphere, cyl, convex, magic), [FONT=Courier New]expand, contract, shift, outset, inset, trim, chunk, count, distr, wer[/FONT]
[*][B]Edit a selection (21):[/B] [FONT=Courier New]set, replace, walls, faces, stack, move, overlay, naturalize, smooth, hollow, center, line, curve, snowsmooth, update, fixblocks, fall, gmask, gsmask, gtransform, gtexture[/FONT]
[*][B]Preview, undo and jobs (8):[/B] [FONT=Courier New]confirm, cancel, undo, redo, history, clearhistory, jobs, limits[/FONT]
[*][B]Copy and schematics (9):[/B] [FONT=Courier New]copy, cut, paste, place, rotate, flip, clearclipboard, schem[/FONT] (save, load, loadall, move, list, delete, import, formats), [FONT=Courier New]structure[/FONT] (the game's own templates)
[*][B]Shapes (7):[/B] [FONT=Courier New]sphere, hsphere, cyl, hcyl, pyramid, hpyramid, cone[/FONT]
[*][B]Terrain (4):[/B] [FONT=Courier New]mountain, island, reroll, styles[/FONT]
[*][B]Biomes, trees, plants and the game's features (8):[/B] [FONT=Courier New]biomelist, biomeinfo, setbiome, forest, forestgen, flora, pumpkins, feature[/FONT]
[*][B]Formulas (5):[/B] [FONT=Courier New]generate, generatebiome, deform, calc, timeout[/FONT]
[*][B]Caves, ores and pictures (4):[/B] [FONT=Courier New]caves, ore, ores, image[/FONT]
[*][B]Fixes around you (14):[/B] [FONT=Courier New]drain, fixwater, fixlava, fill, fillr, removenear, replacenear, removeabove, removebelow, extinguish, snow, thaw, green, fixlighting[/FONT]
[*][B]Entities (2):[/B] [FONT=Courier New]butcher, remove[/FONT]
[*][B]Brushes and tools (12):[/B] [FONT=Courier New]brush[/FONT] (48: sphere, cyl, set, clipboard, splatter, scatter, rock, gravity, extinguish, butcher, forest, deform, snow, snowsmooth, biome, morph, dilate, heightmap, feature, apply … item, paint … item, line, spline, surfacespline, sweep, catenary, circle, pull, recursive, shatter, stencil, image, height, populateschematic, copypaste, savebrush, listbrush, loadbrush, and the terrain brush: raise, lower, smooth, flatten, erode, paint), [FONT=Courier New]tool[/FONT] (14: repl, floodfill, info, cycler, deltree, farwand, lrbuild, navwand, tree, stacker, inspect, featureplacer, structureplacer, none), [FONT=Courier New]superpickaxe[/FONT] (single, area, recursive), [FONT=Courier New]range, tracemask, target, targetoffset, scroll, smask, transform, primary, secondary[/FONT]
[*][B]Where things go (3):[/B] [FONT=Courier New]placement, toggleplace, toggleeditwand[/FONT]
[*][B]Moving around (7):[/B] [FONT=Courier New]unstuck, ascend, descend, ceil, thru, jumpto, up[/FONT]
[*][B]Back to the original (3):[/B] [FONT=Courier New]regen, snapshot, restore[/FONT]
[*][B]Information (10):[/B] [FONT=Courier New]chunkinfo, listchunks, searchitem, version, report, trace, tz, nbtinfo, registry, debugpaste[/FONT]
[*][B]Admin (5):[/B] [FONT=Courier New]help, reload, validate, selftest, wea[/FONT]
[/LIST]
[CODE]/wc wand                                     left click = corner 1, right click = corner 2
/wc set 70% stone, 30% andesite --preview    see it first (only you), then /wc confirm
/wc replace dirt, grass_block with stone
/wc undo                                     works after a restart; leaves alone what others changed since
/wc mountain                                 a mountain where you look: [Build] [Another] [Cancel]
/wc schem load castles/tower                 a WorldEdit .schem into your clipboard, then /wc paste --preview
/wc generate stone x^2+y^2+z^2<1             a shape from a formula, written like in WorldEdit[/CODE]

[SIZE=5][B]What it does better[/B][/SIZE]
[LIST]
[*][B]No lag, ever.[/B] 8 ms of each 50 ms tick for the whole plugin ([FONT=Courier New]performance.max_ms_per_tick[/FONT]); the clock is checked on every block. Two players' edits share the time in turns. Unloaded chunks load in the background.
[*][B]See before you change.[/B] [FONT=Courier New]--preview[/FONT] shows fake blocks only you see; [FONT=Courier New]/wc confirm[/FONT] then does exactly that. Edits over 50 000 blocks ask first.
[*][B]Undo that is not lost.[/B] Each player's history is on disk: undo after a restart or a crash. Blocks somebody changed after your edit are left alone, and you are told how many. Chests and signs come back with their contents.
[*][B]Plain words.[/B] [FONT=Courier New]70% stone, 30% andesite[/FONT], [FONT=Courier New]*_wool, !red_wool[/FONT], [FONT=Courier New]replace dirt with stone[/FONT]. Mistakes are found before anything changes, with "did you mean".
[*][B]Safe limits.[/B] Per permission group: biggest edit, edits at once, worlds and blocked blocks (bedrock, barriers, command blocks and portals are blocked by default except for [FONT=Courier New]admin[/FONT]).
[*][B]For other plugins.[/B] A Java API ([FONT=Courier New]WorldcraftApi.get()[/FONT]: selections, set, replace, paste, undo through the same engine) and a cancellable [FONT=Courier New]WorldcraftEditEvent[/FONT] before every edit, commands included.
[/LIST]

[SIZE=5][B]Permissions[/B][/SIZE]
All [B]op[/B] by default: [FONT=Courier New]worldcraft.use[/FONT] (the wand and every edit on your own selection), [FONT=Courier New]worldcraft.moderate[/FONT] (see and undo other players' edits), [FONT=Courier New]worldcraft.admin[/FONT], [FONT=Courier New]worldcraft.schematic[/FONT], [FONT=Courier New]worldcraft.schematic.save[/FONT], [FONT=Courier New]worldcraft.schematic.delete[/FONT], [FONT=Courier New]worldcraft.butcher[/FONT], [FONT=Courier New]worldcraft.remove[/FONT], [FONT=Courier New]worldcraft.navigate[/FONT], [FONT=Courier New]worldcraft.superpickaxe[/FONT], [FONT=Courier New]worldcraft.image.link[/FONT], [FONT=Courier New]worldcraft.regen[/FONT], [FONT=Courier New]worldcraft.snapshot[/FONT], and [FONT=Courier New]worldcraft.limit.<group>[/FONT] for the limits of a group in config.yml.

[SIZE=5][B]Compatibility[/B][/SIZE]
[LIST]
[*][B]Paper 1.21.4:[/B] verified (unit tests, a real server and an in-game test suite with bots). Other Paper 1.21.x and 26.x: not verified yet.
[*][B]Java 21+.[/B] [B]Paper only:[/B] not Spigot/CraftBukkit, not Folia.
[*][B]No dependencies.[/B] It can run next to WorldEdit (different command and wand). WorldGuard and PlotSquared use WorldEdit's own API, so keep WorldEdit installed if you use them.
[*]No network access, unless you turn on picture links ([FONT=Courier New]images.links[/FONT], off by default).
[/LIST]

