[SPOILER="Image transcription"]
[B]Header.[/B] Worldcraft. Edit the world. Never freeze the server. WorldEdit's commands under /wc, run in small batches that never lag. Preview every edit, undo it after a restart, and make a mountain with one word. Paper 1.21.4 · 138 commands · No WorldEdit needed · Reads .schem.

[B]A mountain in one word.[/B] /wc mountain large and /wc island large: a mountain with snowy peaks and a floating island with trees over a generated plain. Shown first: [Build] [Another] [Cancel].

[B]Shapes, pictures, formulas.[/B] The commands builders already know, with --preview: only you see it until /wc confirm. /wc sphere orange_concrete 9, /wc hcyl light_blue_concrete 8 16: a sphere, a hollow cylinder, a pyramid and a cone. /wc image logo.png 48, /wc generate stone x^2+y^2+z^2<1: the Worldcraft logo built with blocks.

[B]Worldcraft vs WorldEdit vs FAWE.[/B] The same comparison as the list above. Worldcraft 0.16.0, WorldEdit 7.3.19, FAWE 2.16.2 (November 2026).

[B]How many commands?[/B] 138 commands under /wc (212 counted like WorldEdit counts its own). 157 of WorldEdit's 171: the same or better (92 %), 5 more in part. 205 of FAWE's 244: the same or better (84 %), 13 more in part. Then the command names by group, as in the list above.

[B]What it does better.[/B] No lag, ever: every edit runs in batches inside 8 ms of each tick, for the whole plugin; two players share it in turns. Preview, then confirm: --preview shows fake blocks only you see; edits over 50 000 blocks ask first. Undo that is not lost: history on disk, undo after a restart or a crash; what others built since is left alone. Plain words: replace dirt with 70% stone, 30% andesite; typos get "did you mean", before anything changes. Safe by default: limits per permission group; nobody places bedrock or command blocks unless you allow it. For other plugins: a Java API and a cancellable WorldcraftEditEvent before every edit.

[B]How to start.[/B] 1. Drop the jar in plugins/ (Paper 1.21.4, Java 21). 2. /wc wand, then click two corners. 3. /wc set stone --preview and /wc confirm. 4. /wc undo, even after a restart.
[/SPOILER]
